  "title": "The reach on ladders and grids",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "The reach on ladders and grids (computation with a validated pipeline). With the Fano plane attached at a point of a plane piece and the removal inside it, creation at each plane gluing line was decided by ticket A's route criterion over pairs of handle points, with every transfer computed by heights (ticket B). On small spaces this pipeline equals exact creation in all 2,784 cases, and the fast splice equals glue_lib.splice in all 10 spaces. Ladders (prisms over 2k-cycles, 10 to 80 points): the halo reaches the farthest gluing line at every size (reach 5 to 41, growing linearly), with exactly two of the four gluing lines creating at each distance. Only the far sides K4^(3) and census 6 create beyond the lines through the cut. Grids (duals of the octahedron subdivided once to three times, 16 to 256 points, several attachment points): the reach is exactly 3. The forcing profile explains the split. On the ladder, fixing the split point's three copies leaves every gluing line at distance 3 or more with exactly two patterns. On the grids, every gluing line at distance 7 or more has the full transfer (all 36 pairs), so it is exactly independent of the split point. Random grown spaces (20 to 40 points) reach 5 to 7.",
